    "result_text": "The full test suite is green \u2014 there are only 3 test files (`AcceptanceTest` plus two support classes `AcceptanceBase` and `AuditLogCapture`), so `AcceptanceTest` is the entire runnable suite, and it passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the GOLD membership tier rule. The membership tier is a derived value computed at DTO-mapping time in `OwnerMapper`, so that's where the rule lives.\n\n**Change** \u2014 `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java`:\n- Converted the mapper from an `interface` to an `abstract class` (MapStruct supports both; the generated `OwnerMapperImpl` extends it) so it can hold an injected dependency.\n- Injected `ClinicService` via an `@Autowired` field (Spring autowires the inherited field on the generated `@Component` subclass \u2014 the project sets `mapstruct.defaultComponentModel=spring`). No circular dependency, since `ClinicServiceImpl` depends only on repositories.\n- Added a `householdSize(owner)` helper that counts owners sharing the same `householdId`, and made `membershipTier(owner)` return `\"GOLD\"` when that count is \u2265 3, otherwise falling through to the existing SILVER/BRONZE logic unchanged.\n\nThe tier is computed live against the current household, so it correctly reflects \"3 or more members after this create\" at both the create response and subsequent `GET /api/owners/{id}` \u2014 which is what the `coreGoldForThreeMemberHousehold` test asserts. No entity or schema changes were needed (`householdId` is already set during create in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`).",
